"menu-item-54\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-taxonomy menu-item-object-category menu-item-54\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/category/news/\">Recent News</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-8507\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-8507\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/newsletters/moruya-mail/\">Moruya Mail</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-17\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-has-children menu-item-17\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/\">About</a>\n<ul class=\"sub-menu\">\n<li id=\"menu-item-107\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-107\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/people/\">People</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-2136\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-2136\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/shasa-helping-change-happen/\">Making Change Happen</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-8768\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-8768\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/shasa-achievements/\">SHASA Achievements</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-8794\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-8794\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/shasa-resilience-awards/\">SHASA Resilience Awards</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-2800\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-2800\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/volunteer/\">Volunteer</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-106\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-106\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/contact/\">Contact</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-6171\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-6171\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/membership-and-donations/\">Join &#038; Donate</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-11051\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-11051\"><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/governance/\">Governance</a></li>\n</ul></div>		</nav><!-- #site-navigation -->\n</div>\n</div>\n<a class=\"skip-link screen-reader-text\" href=\"#content\">Skip to content</a>\n<!-- Full Banner Image -->\n<!-- END Full Banner Image -->\n<div class=\"bkg clearfix\">\n<div id=\"content\" class=\"clearfix\">\n<main class=\"content-nosidebar\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\">Community Solar Installations</h1>				\n<p>Community not for profit organisations struggle with ongoing static operating costs such as electricity, so in 2017 SHASA joined forces with Micro Energy Systems Australia (MESA) to support these community not for profit organisations and assist their transition to a clean energy future.   The partnership between MESA and SHASA has resulted in many successful community solar installations through either:</p>\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Fully gifting Photo Voltaic Solar systems free of charge to community not for profit organisations.</li>\n<li>Sourcing grants to support the installation of Photo Voltaic Solar systems to community not for profit organisations.</li>\n<li>Supporting community organisations to install Photo Voltaic Solar systems through our Eurobodalla Solar Bulk Buy program.   </li>\n</ol>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Community facility partnerships summary</h2>\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The Eurobodalla Solar Bulk Buy partnership between Micro Energy Systems Australia and SHASA has resulted in <strong>gifting the full funds to install solar</strong> on the following community facilities:</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table is-style-regular\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/energy/community-solar-installations/moruyas-red-door-solar/\">Red Door</a> Hall, Anglican Parish, Moruya</td><td>3.48kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Nov 2018</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-499\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/red-door.jpg\" alt=\"red door\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/red-door.jpg 1296w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/red-door-300x224.jpg 300w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/red-door-1024x765.jpg 1024w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/red-door-768x574.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/energy/community-solar-installations/montys-place-narooma-goes-solar/\">Montys Place</a>, Uniting Church of Australia, Narooma</td><td>5.4kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">April 2019</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/montys-place-1-rotated.jpg\" alt=\"montys place-1 rotated\" style=\"width: 150px;\"></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/moruya-bushfire-and-heatwave-haven/\">Moruya Bushfire and Heatwave Haven</a>, Anglican Parish, Moruya</td><td>6.3kW PV Solar System with Battery Storage system  &amp; more!</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Jan 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-964\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Moruya-Heatwave-Shelter.jpg\" alt=\"Moruya Heatwave Shelter\"></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/energy/community-solar-installations/bodalla-local-aboriginal-land-council/\">Bodalla Local Aboriginal Lands Council</a>, Bodalla</td><td>6.3kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">May 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"131\" class=\"wp-image-808\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/A-partnership-for-a-cleaner-future.jpg\" alt=\"A-partnership for a cleaner future\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/A-partnership-for-a-cleaner-future.jpg 1024w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/A-partnership-for-a-cleaner-future-300x261.jpg 300w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/A-partnership-for-a-cleaner-future-768x669.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/SEWACS-Media-Release.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">South East Women and Children&#8217;s Services </a>(SEWACS), Moruya</td><td>6.3kW PV Solar System 3 phase</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Nov 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"113\" class=\"wp-image-2011\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/cafd4488-b2c4-4f8a-a1d7-375cdd1b8595.jpg\" alt=\"6.3kW PV Solar System 3 phase\"></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>2.  SHASA and MESA have assisted the following community groups to successfully apply for<strong> grant funding</strong> for solar installations on their community facilities:</p>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td>Batemans Bay Surf Life Saving Club in Malua Bay</td><td>12.82kW PV Solar System </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Sept 2018</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-795\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/BB-Surf-Lifesaving-Club.jpg\" alt=\"BB Surf Lifesaving Club\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/BB-Surf-Lifesaving-Club.jpg 640w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/BB-Surf-Lifesaving-Club-300x224.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>Rally for Recovery Tomakin</td><td>5.6kW PV Solar System </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Sept 2018</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-938\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/IMG_9662.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_9662\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/IMG_9662.jpg 640w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/IMG_9662-300x224.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>Country Women&#8217;s Association (CWA) Surf Beach Batemans Bay</td><td>5kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2018</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-937\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/CWA-Batemans-Bay-rotated.jpg\" alt=\"CWA Batemans Bay rotated\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/CWA-Batemans-Bay-rotated.jpg 640w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/CWA-Batemans-Bay-300x224.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>Narooma Men&#8217;s Shed, Narooma</td><td>9.45kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"113\" class=\"wp-image-1784\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Narooma-Mens-shed-2.jpg\" alt=\"Narooma Mens shed\"></td></tr><tr><td>Bateman&#8217;s Bay Men&#8217;s Shed, Batemans Bay</td><td>9.8kW PV Solar System using micro inverters</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"113\" class=\"wp-image-1785\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/BB-Mens-shed.jpg\" alt=\"BB Mens shed\"></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Narooma-Marine-Rescue-media-release.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Narooma Marine Rescue</a>, Narooma</td><td>6.3kW PV Solar System with 6.3kWh battery storage</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">April 2021</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/IMG_7699.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_7699\" style=\"width: 155px;\"></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://aboutregional.com.au/moruya-preschool-well-on-the-way-to-becoming-a-true-bushfire-safe-haven/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Moruya Pre School Kindergarten Bushfire &amp; Heatwave Haven</a></td><td>9.8kW PV Solar System with 11.6kWh battery storage &amp; more!</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">July 2021</span></td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"100\" class=\"wp-image-3510\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/IMG_1801-640x427-1.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_1801\"></td></tr><tr><td>Country Women&#8217;s Association (CWA), <br>Moruya</td><td>Lighting &amp; Electrical Upgrade</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Feb 2022</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Federal Powering Communities grant</td></tr><tr><td>Tilba Halls, <br>Central Tilba</td><td>Redevelopment, Heatwave Haven &amp; EV Charging Station</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color\">In progress</span></strong></td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">BLERF grant <br>approved July 2021</td></tr><tr><td>Country Women&#8217;s Association (CWA), Narooma</td><td>Redevelopment &amp; Heatwave Haven </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color\">In progress</span></strong><br></td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">NSW Community Infrastructure &amp; Disaster grant approved Nov 2021</td></tr><tr><td>Country Women&#8217;s Association (CWA), <br>Moruya</td><td>Bushfire and Heatwave Haven</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"> <strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color\">In progress</span></strong></td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"> Federal Black Summer grant approved Feb 2022 </td></tr><tr><td>Narooma Men&#8217;s Shed, <br>Narooma</td><td>Bushfire and Heatwave Haven</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"> <strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color\">In progress</span></strong> </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Federal Black Summer grant approved Feb 2022</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color\"><strong>New!</strong></span><br>Uniting Church, <br>Batemans Bay</td><td>Bushfire and Heatwave Haven</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color\"><strong>Just Announced!</strong></span></td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Federal Preparing Australian Communities grant approved April 2022</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>3.  The following organisations have installed solar as part of SHASA&#8217;s<strong> Eurobodalla Solar Bulk Buy</strong>:</p>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td>Gallery Bodalla</td><td>4.4kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2017</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Gallery-Bodalla-scaled.jpg\" alt=\"Gallery Bodalla\" style=\"width: 150px;\"></td></tr><tr><td>Muddy Puddles, Catalina</td><td>36.4kW PV Solar System </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">May 2018</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"wp-image-774\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Muddy-Puddles-1.jpg\" alt=\"Muddy Puddles\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Muddy-Puddles-1.jpg 640w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Muddy-Puddles-1-300x300.jpg 300w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Muddy-Puddles-1-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>Narooma Sport &amp; Game Fishing Club, Narooma</td><td>5.67kW PV Solar System </td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2019</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-771\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/fishing-club-1.jpg\" alt=\"fishing club\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/fishing-club-1.jpg 1296w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/fishing-club-1-300x224.jpg 300w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/fishing-club-1-1024x765.jpg 1024w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/fishing-club-1-768x574.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>Kyla Park Community Hall, Tuross Head</td><td>10.8kW PV Solar System</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Oct 2019</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"112\" class=\"wp-image-772\" style=\"width: 150px;\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/kyla-park-1.jpg\" alt=\"kyla park\" srcset=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/kyla-park-1.jpg 1296w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/kyla-park-1-300x224.jpg 300w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/kyla-park-1-1024x765.jpg 1024w, https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/kyla-park-1-768x574.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></td></tr><tr><td>1st Bateman&#8217;s Bay Scout Group, Bateman&#8217;s Bay</td><td>12.6kW PV Solar System with 6.3kW battery storage</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Sept 2020</td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/1st-Batemans-Bay-Scouts-Group.jpg\" alt=\"1st Batemans Bay Scouts Group\" style=\"width: 150px;\"></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>Please <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/about-us/contact/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">contact us</a> if your community group is interested in partnering with SHASA to apply for a grant to install solar for your facility.   We look forward to supporting more community facilities across the Eurobodalla. </p>\n</main><!-- #main -->\n\n</div><!-- #content -->\n<div class=\"centercta\">\n<div class=\"centercta-holdit\">\n<p><strong>Sign up</strong> and join with more than 500 supporters from across the Eurobodalla Shire and beyond to help co-create an inspiring and resilient future for the region.</p>\n<div class=\"wpcf7 no-js\" id=\"wpcf7-f12091-o1\" lang=\"en-AU\" dir=\"ltr\" data-wpcf7-id=\"1